{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "def is_samepatterns(array1, array2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if two arrays of strings follow the same pattern of repeated elements.\n    It establishes a one-to-one mapping and ensures consistency throughout the arrays.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(array1) != len(array2):\n        return False\n\n    # Mappings for one-to-one correspondence\n    map1_to_2 = {}\n    map2_to_1 = {}\n\n    for i in range(len(array1)):\n        elem1 = array1[i]\n        elem2 = array2[i]\n\n        # Check mapping from array1 to array2\n        if elem1 in map1_to_2:\n            if map1_to_2[elem1] != elem2:\n                return False\n        else:\n            map1_to_2[elem1] = elem2\n\n        # Check mapping from array2 to array1\n        if elem2 in map2_to_1:\n            if map2_to_1[elem2] != elem1:\n                return False\n        else:\n            map2_to_1[elem2] = elem1\n\n    return True"}
