{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence.\n    P(1) = 1, P(2) = 1, P(n) = P(P(n-1)) + P(n - P(n-1)) for n > 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 1 or n == 2:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize a list to store the sequence values, 1-indexed\n    p = [0] * (n + 1)\n    p[1] = 1\n    p[2] = 1\n\n    # Compute the sequence iteratively\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        p[i] = p[p[i - 1]] + p[i - p[i - 1]]\n\n    return p[n]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/77", "solution": "def is_Diff(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number is divisible by 11 using the alternating sum of its digits.\n    Negative numbers are treated as their absolute value.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_abs = abs(number)\n    s_num = str(num_abs)\n    \n    alternating_sum = 0\n    # Calculate the alternating sum of digits from right to left.\n    for i, digit_char in enumerate(reversed(s_num)):\n        digit = int(digit_char)\n        if i % 2 == 0:\n            alternating_sum += digit\n        else:\n            alternating_sum -= digit\n            \n    return alternating_sum % 11 == 0"}
